      "key": {
        "uuid": "678ed9d9_0ee6f363",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Nat464Xlat.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-04T08:21:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do we do about the LinkProperties here?\n\nIf this stop is due to a disconnect, updating them is not necessary. But if this call to stop() is due to clatd being no longer needed (e.g., if IPv4 address appears), then CS (and netd) will still think that we have a stacked interface, even though we don\u0027t any more because clatd has been stopped. I think we handle this case correctly today (modulo the race we\u0027re trying to fix, of course).\n\nNot sure how to fix this.\n\nThe simplest thing would be to update the LinkProperties if we\u0027re in state RUNNING, but I\u0027m not sure that\u0027s safe to do if we\u0027re being called from handleAsyncChannelDisconnected. It looks like we\u0027d at least send out an onLinkPropertiesChanged after onLost, which I don\u0027t think we do at the moment.\n\nMaybe we can make handleUpdateLinkProperties call isLiveNetworkAgent as discussed previously. I think this should be safe because maybeHandleNetworkAgentMessage, which is the only caller of handleUpdateLinkProperties, already performs a very similar check.\n\nOr maybe we can make handleUpdateLinkProperties ignore updates if the network is in state DISCONNECTED. This seems like a bigger change.\n\nOr maybe CS can pass in a boolean indicating this call to stop() is due to a teardown.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "24a68455b79298a1d9fe1a7213d7a10191604857",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e029d21a_32dce93a",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Nat464Xlat.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-04T08:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another way that might be simpler and less risky than the above:\n\n    // Unless the network is being torn down, tell ConnectivityService that\n    // our stacked link is gone. This relies on the fact that\n    // handleAsyncChannelDisconnected sets the state to\n    / DISCONNECTED before calling stop().\n    if (isRunning() \u0026\u0026 mNetwork.networkInfo.state !\u003d NetworkInfo.State.DISCONNECTED) {\n        LinkProperties lp \u003d new LinkProperties(mNetwork.linkProperties);\n        lp.removeStackedLink(iface);\n        mNetwork.connService().handleUpdateLinkProperties(mNetwork, lp);\n    }\n\n    enterIdleState();",
      "parentUuid": "678ed9d9_0ee6f363",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "24a68455b79298a1d9fe1a7213d7a10191604857",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddcb4729_4b698485",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Nat464Xlat.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-04T13:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But if this call to stop() is due to clatd being no longer needed (e.g., if IPv4 address appears), then CS (and netd) will still think that we have a stacked interface, even though we don\u0027t any more because clatd has been stopped. \n\nWell spotted, I missed that case.\n\n\n\u003e Maybe we can make handleUpdateLinkProperties call isLiveNetworkAgent as discussed previously.\n\nI don\u0027t like these kind of solutions because to me these are anti-patterns that increase the assumptions about various side-effects at different point in the state evolution of these classes.\n\n\u003e if (isRunning() \u0026\u0026 mNetwork.networkInfo.state !\u003d NetworkInfo.State.DISCONNECTED) {\n\nditto\n\n\n\u003e Or maybe CS can pass in a boolean indicating this call to stop() is due to a teardown.\n\n+1. That\u0027s much better imo to let the caller specify its intent. Now that I did a bit of refactoring of the callers of Nat464Xlat, that\u0027s actually straightforward to do.\n\nIn addition:\n  - the notification should be reposted on the handler, because otherwise it creates a look back into updateLinkProperties().\n  - the notification even if asked should only fire if Nat464Xlat is in Running state. i.e if the up notification from netd has not arrive, do not update.",
      "parentUuid": "e029d21a_32dce93a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 25
      },
